cted elsewhere rather than\nsupporting duplicative and unnecessary evaluations.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n(2011-12) A.8308 Amend and recommit to Mental Health\n\n(2013-14) A5187 Referred to Mental Health\n(2015-16) A2986 Referred to Mental Health\n2017-18: A6614 Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
